/-!
# Finite modules over a Noetherian ring

Stacks 00IK has three parts, all for a finite module `M` over a Noetherian ring `R`. That `M`
is of finite presentation is `Module.finitePresentation_of_finite`. The other two go through
`isNoetherian_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite`, which says `M` is a Noetherian module: its
submodules are then finitely generated by `IsNoetherian.noetherian`, which is the second part,
and `>` is well-founded on them by `isNoetherian_iff'`, which is the third.

The Artin–Tate lemma, Stacks 00IS, is `fg_of_fg_of_fg`, stated with the finite generation of
`⊤` in place of the `Algebra.FiniteType` and `Module.Finite` classes.
-/

@[expose] public section

add_to_stacks 00IK "(1)" Module.finitePresentation_of_finite
add_to_stacks 00IK "(2) and (3): a finite module over a Noetherian ring is Noetherian"
  isNoetherian_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite
add_to_sga "6 I 1.3" "more general" isNoetherian_of_isNoetherianRing_of_finite
add_to_stacks 00IK "(2): the submodules of a Noetherian module are finitely generated"
  IsNoetherian.noetherian
add_to_stacks 00IK "(3): a Noetherian module satisfies the ascending chain condition on
  submodules" isNoetherian_iff'
